{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"f6e11667e0026ab1","x":-560,"y":-800,"width":560,"height":1480,"type":"text","text":"# Cassian Vael\n#### Position: Headmaster\n- Appointed: ???\n- Age: ???\n\nCassian has held the position of Headmaster for a uniquely long period of time. His personnel file lists an age that doesn’t match his face, but nobody seems to press him on it. He moves through the school halls with the unhurried ease of someone who has simply *stopped* being surprised, as though he may have seen all the world has to offer.\n### Design\nHe is tall and lean. Not imposing in a physical sense – he doesn’t tend to fill a room the way a broad-shouldered person does. He fills it differently. There is a stillness to how he carries himself that makes people away of his presence before they’ve even consciously acknowledged that he’s there.\n#### Features\nHe has deep brown skin with a warm undertone. The kind of complexion that makes his age even harder to clock. His hair is short, with very clean lines. Black with the faintest threading of silver at the temples – subtle enough that it reads more like light than color.\n\nEyes are a deep brown, almost black. Calm in a way that can read as either reassuring of unsettling depending on the circumstances. He doesn’t tend to stare – he instead *regards*.\n#### Facial Hair\nThe mustache he sports sits neat and deliberate above his lip, not thick but well-defined. The goatee is long and thin, coming to a soft point – kept with obvious intention. It’s groomed the way everything about him is groomed: precise without calling attention to itself.\n#### Clothing\nHis suits are impeccable. Dark navy pinstripe, cut slim, never a thread out of place. The half-cape that drapes over his right shoulder is the one concession to someone a bit older – it’s fabric deep as the night sky, with what look like stars drifting slowly across it whenever it catches the light. Students debate endlessly whether it’s enchanted or a trick of the material. He neither confirms nor denies any statements as such.\n\n\n### Personality\nHe is not warm, exactly. But he is *fair*, in a way that seems almost architectural – like fairness is built into how he operates rather than something he chooses in the moment. He rarely raises his voice. He doesn’t usually need to."},
		{"id":"bc96bac64cea9e7a","type":"text","text":"# Aldric Burr\n#### Position: Dean of Student Affairs\n- Appointed: 2009\n- Age: 52\n\nAldric has occupied the role of Deal of Student Affairs long enough that he has mistaken longevity for legacy. He is the Sanctum’s most vocal champion of the Ring system – not because anyone asked him to be, but because he has decided, somewhere deep and unexamined, that this hierarchy is a natural order rather than an arbitrary one. This makes his treatment of Third Ring students feel righteous in his own eyes. Which is, in some ways, worse than simple cruelty.\n### Design\nHe is short and round, carrying his weight like a man who believes other people should be impressed by his stature. He does not move with stillness, instead moving with momentum – the kind that comes from someone who is always slightly more convinced of his own importance than anyone else in the room.\n#### Features\nHis skin is pale with a ruddy, perpetually flushed quality – the kind of complexion that betrays every emotion before he’s chosen to display it. His eyes are small, but a bright golden brown, like a raging fire yearning for some twisted sense of justice. His brow sets his eyes a touch too close together, quick to narrow when someone displeases him – which happens quite often. His nose is broad and sits slightly crooked, and there are rumors that it was a student who broke it once and it never properly healed.\n\nHis hairline is a source of ongoing personal anguish. A widow’s peak so dramatic it reads as almost aggressive advances down his forehead, and he has trimmed every two weeks in a losing battle to make it look intentional. It does not. The hair that remains is a dark brown, oiled flat against his scalp with something that smells faintly medicinal.\n#### Facial Hair\nThe mustache and thin goatee he sports are clearly inspired by the headmaster – a fact that the entire faculty has noticed yet no one mentions to his face. On Vael, the style is precise without calling attention to itself. On Burr, it looks researched. The goatee in particular never quite comes to a clean point, and the mustache sits a fraction too thick, as though he’s been incrementally adjusting it towards something he saw and couldn’t fully replicate.\n#### Clothing\nBurr wears the faculty dress uniform as though it were a costume he hasn’t quite grown into. Everything fits a size too snug across the middle, and his collar always looks like it’s losing an argument with his neck. He favors a deep burgundy and dark olive to match with the crimson of the school colors – rich colors that he believes project authority. They instead project much effort.\n### Personality\nHe is not EVIL. He is something arguably more tiresome: a man of middling power who has mistaken his prejudices for principles. His favoritism towards the First Ring students is not subtle – it functions as unofficial policy, operating in the comfortable space between unwritten and unaddressed. He is loud in faculty meetings, overbearing in the halls, and oddly quiet whenever headmaster Vael is in the room.\n\n#### Relationships\nHis relationship with the Headmaster is best descripted as Burr believing they are close confidants, and Vael treating him like a piece of furniture that occasionally needs to be polished.","x":80,"y":-800,"width":560,"height":1920}
	],
	"edges":[]
}